*.test
# Credentials. None of these may ever be committed, and the leak gate
# treats a match as a finding rather than something to review.
client_secret*.json
token.json
.env
# The editor writes its settings, and temporary copies of them, into the
# working tree while a session runs, so a wildcard `git add` takes
# whatever exists at that instant. A tool that writes here needs its rule
# before the first wildcard add, not after the first one is committed —
# which is how a stray file reached a sibling project's public history.
# Locally these are also covered by a global ignore; a contributor
# cloning this repository has no such protection, which is why the rule
# lives here.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.tmp.*
